x A first-block `[^a]: +` or `> +` needs a flush follower.

[^a]: +
  x   ^ -markup.list.continuation.carve

[^a]: +
x     ^ markup.list.continuation.carve

> +
x ^ markup.list.continuation.carve

> +
  x <- -markup.list.continuation.carve

x An indented `>` line outside a list item opens no quote, so its `+` is text
x whatever follows (spec row 630-10). Under a list item it stays a marker.

  > +
x   ^ -markup.list.continuation.carve

 > > +
x    ^ -markup.list.continuation.carve

::: note
  > +
x   ^ -markup.list.continuation.carve
:::

[^a]: a
  > +
x   ^ -markup.list.continuation.carve

- a
  > +
x   ^ markup.list.continuation.carve

x A chain ending in a quote marker inside a quote takes a non-list block at
x column 0 (spec row 655), and a `+` at column 0 below an item's indented
x quote is at the item's column (spec row 635).

> - > +
x     ^ markup.list.continuation.carve

